# Git — commit and push after changes

After completing any task that modifies project files:

1. Run `git status` and `git diff` to review changes.
2. Stage only relevant files (never `.env`, credentials, `*.rar`, web export artifacts).
3. Create a concise commit with a clear message (why, not just what).
4. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).

Do this without waiting for a separate "push" request, unless the user explicitly says not to commit yet.

Remote: https://github.com/limbo1572/vibe-coder-room (public, branch `main`).

Do not force-push to `main`. Do not update git config.
